><highlight color="#9643FC" opacity="0.399994" creationdate="D:20250509102619+10'00'" flags="print" IT="HighlightNote" date="D:20250509102624+10'00'" name="20e20ea0-bab7-416f-a6a4-b6a8f0236ab1" page="5" coords="36.000000,571.853760,298.985840,571.853760,36.000000,560.823853,298.985840,560.823853,36.000000,560.855713,298.941101,560.855713,36.000000,549.825745,298.941101,549.825745,36.000000,549.857544,298.929871,549.857544,36.000000,538.827637,298.929871,538.827637,36.000000,538.859497,299.028687,538.859497,36.000000,527.829529,299.028687,527.829529,36.000000,527.861328,298.924683,527.861328,36.000000,516.831421,298.924683,516.831421,36.000000,516.863281,298.927551,516.863281,36.000000,505.833313,298.927551,505.833313,35.999985,505.865143,298.960632,505.865143,35.999985,494.835205,298.960632,494.835205,35.999985,494.867035,299.010895,494.867035,35.999985,483.837097,299.010895,483.837097,35.999985,483.868927,299.006989,483.868927,35.999985,472.838989,299.006989,472.838989,36.000000,472.870819,298.966187,472.870819,36.000000,461.840881,298.966187,461.840881" rect="35.655289,461.496185,299.373383,572.198486" subject="Comment on Text" title="alexd"
><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:25.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Q14c: </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-13.3pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>The findings from this study suggest that there is not a typical&#xD;muscle fiber typology (MFT) best suited to the sport of Australian&#xD;football (AF) or a position-specific MFT within AF. However,&#xD;most athletes had negative CAZ-score values, which is indicative&#xD;of a greater estimated proportion of type I fibers. A greater&#xD;estimated proportion of type I fibers was associated with greater&#xD;high-speed-running distance during match play and an enhanced&#xD;capacity to maintain high-speed running during peak periods of&#xD;increasing duration. These findings highlight the importance of&#xD;MFT in relation to key GNSS-derived metrics of AF match play.</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="5" rect="612.128723,275.565491,796.055359,572.073486"
/></highlight
